==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈprɛnːa/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ɛnːa|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|is|non|brinna}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*brinnaną}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-strong|brann|brunnu|brunnið}}

# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[burn]], to be [[on fire]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{is-conj-s3|br|e|nn|mp=-}}

=====Derived terms=====
* [[brunninn]]
* [[brenna allar brýr að baki sér]]
* [[brenna við]] (to get burned)
*: ''Maturinn '''brann við'''.''
*:: The food '''got burned'''.
* [[vilja brenna við]] (to tend to happen)
*: ''Það '''vill brenna við'''.''
*:: It '''tends to happen'''.''
* [[brenna í skinninu]] (to be [[raring]] to go)
*: ''Hann '''brennur í skinninu'''.''
*:: He's '''raring to go'''.''
* [[láta sér ekki allt fyrir brjósti brenna]] (to be not afraid of anything)

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|is|non|brenna}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*brannijaną}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-weak|brenndi|brennt}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[burn]], to [[set on fire]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég '''brenndi''' mig á fingrinum!|I '''burnt''' my finger!}}
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the dative}} to heat up with
#: {{ux|is|Að '''brenna''' [[kol]]um.|To '''heat up with''' [[coal]]s.}}

=====Derived terms=====
* [[brenndur]]

===Etymology 3===

====Noun====
{{is-noun|f|brennu|brennur}}

# [[burning]]
# [[bonfire]]
#: {{ux|is|Hvenær byrjar '''brennan'''?|When does the '''bonfire''' start?}}

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-f-w1|br|e|nn}}

